{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 2b80f0e1d8b65fe9cad4b2eaa20825897c6575ea on builder/kd1-down-label-race-20261118, all 5 artifacts, for request c5357a96 under my promise 823076fa. The implementation is KD-1 (request 2cc0c0b2, promise c09b69fa). The reporting artifact is the KD-1 note.\n\nThe head's parent is 7cb207e1. Main has since moved to 7dc016cf (U2), which changes no path under `apps/room/celld/mac` or `docs`. `git merge-tree --write-tree 7dc016cf 2b80f0e1` merges cleanly to tree 8008342e.\n\n## What I read\n\n- The note first, then the whole diff.\n- `kit.py` moves launchctl's missing-label answer (exit status 113 with `Could not find service \"\u003clabel\u003e\"` on stderr) into `service_missing`. `job_state` keeps the same behavior.\n- `shutdown.py`: `MacPorts.job` answers `(\"absent\", None)` when its second `launchctl print` gives that exact answer. Any other failure of the second read still raises \"supervisor became unavailable\". The match needs both the status and the label text, so a different 113 still refuses, and the second test proves that.\n- `bootout` still requires proof of closure. An absent label completes the closure only when `identity(original.pid)` no longer equals the original identity (`shutdown.py:193`). So the new `absent` answer cannot pass off a live process as closed. If the race hits the first `job` read in `bootout` while `known` is None, `bootout` still refuses with \"service process identity unavailable\". That fails closed and leaves the store running, as before. The 18:33 log puts the race in the polling loop after the `bootout` command, which this fix covers.\n- The guide. `main` returns 0 only when `preservePreparation` is `complete` and `storeStopped` is true (`shutdown.py:277`). So the new guide text is true, and the sentence it removes contradicted the code. The guide tells the owner to run the start lines only after exit status 0, and to keep and report the JSON line otherwise. It also explains the `5: Input/output error` that the owner saw.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- The red. `artroom-evidence/2026-11-18-kd1-red/red.txt` ends in `kit.Refusal: supervisor became unavailable`, and its SHA-256 begins `ed0b32ff`, as the note says.\n- The gate. END 3e74ebe5 passed at this head. The first line of `artroom-evidence/2026-11-18-kd1-gate/gate.txt` names this head with 0 changed files, and the log ends \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 5 artifacts name the head and equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 7cb207e1 2b80f0e1`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n- Wake rate. The head adds no alarm, retry or scheduled pass. The polling loop in `bootout` keeps its deadline and its 0.25-second sleep.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One shared predicate names launchctl's missing-label answer for both reads.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change accepts only launchctl's exact missing-label answer. The closure still requires the original process to be gone, and every other failure still stops the procedure before it stops the store.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThe installed kit under `/Library/dap-host` changes only when the owner installs it again after landing. This approval authorizes no push, landing, install or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:55695aeb4f1daf3e995ef5b4076ba05859b6bdd8","binding":"assigned","head":"2b80f0e1d8b65fe9cad4b2eaa20825897c6575ea","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:823076fa1b8c53bcdc942684e83fb43022314d12\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c09b69faebac5bbe4c4613b932ecbf8a493c1d1e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:823076fa1b8c53bcdc942684e83fb43022314d12","review_path":"reviewguard@1","ve